<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i) == c.toArray()[i];</code>--------------------<code>assert c != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i) == c.toArray()[i];</code>--------------------<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result; this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

However, since `\result` refers to the return value of the method and the method does not return anything (it's a constructor), we should use the size of the list instead. Therefore, the correct assert statement would be:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>--------------------